// Title: Enable Remote Connection Between Anonymous Computer - AllowAnonymousCallback
// Sigma ID: 4d431012-2ab5-4db7-a84e-b29809da2172
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-11-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects enabling of the "AllowAnonymousCallback" registry value, which allows a remote
//   connection between computers that do not have a trust relationship.
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/wmisdk/connecting-to-wmi-remotely-starting-with-vista
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_set_enable_anonymous_connection.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\WBEM\\CIMOM\\AllowAnonymousCallback" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
